# DSL and Shell Features Demo
# Demonstrates Using { } blocks and shell command execution.

# --- DSL Block Example: Simple Make-like rule parser ---

To ProcessRules a Source:
    Print "Processing DSL rules:" followed by Source.
    Print "Rule count: 3 items processed".
    Print "DSL parsed successfully".

# The DSL content between { } is passed as raw text to ProcessRules.
Using ProcessRules parse {
    build: main.o util.o
        gcc -o build main.o util.o

    main.o: main.c
        gcc -c main.c
}

# --- Shell Command Execution ---

# Execute a shell command (output goes to stdout).
Execute the shell command `echo Hello from the OS shell!`.

# Execute another command.
Execute the shell command `node --version`.

# --- Capturing Shell Output ---

A Text named SystemInfo exists.
SystemInfo is `echo Prose-OS-Integration`.

Print "Captured output:" followed by SystemInfo.
